message: >-
  If you use Activation Energy Studio, cite this software release and the
  original dataset or article used for every included real-data example.
title: Activation Energy Studio
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Solak
    given-names: Mehmet
    affiliation: Biosystems Engineering, Siirt University, Siirt, Türkiye
version: 0.4.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A local-first browser application for evidence-grounded apparent
  activation-energy analysis of multi-rate thermoanalytical data using FWO,
  KAS, Starink, Friedman, and a separate beta-Tp Kissinger workflow.
keywords:
  - activation energy
  - thermogravimetric analysis
  - isoconversional kinetics
  - FWO
  - KAS
  - Starink
  - Friedman
  - Kissinger
